                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "85e525bb-d5ac-49f4-aa6d-1ac0028550f8",
                                "sense_id": "b1c1ecf4-bb55-350b-a9e4-4dabe02f6269",
                                "text": "A woodhouse is rightly a house for wood, and a woodenhouse one made of wood; a paper bag, a bag for papers, and a papern bag, one made of paper; an iron tool, one for working in iron, and an ironen tool, one of iron, and so on."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f6a20651-8e67-4e69-a7e5-ce9dfe91d584",
                                "sense_id": "b1c1ecf4-bb55-350b-a9e4-4dabe02f6269",
                                "text": "Put thare ta draw things out a Jan; An thit twis bit a papern wal, Zo thit tha witch cude yer et al, An, wen Jan enter'd tother dore, Cude tul min aul ha'd naw'd avaur ;— [...]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d7a36c60-0c90-42ee-a22d-8e9511104e32",
                                "sense_id": "b1c1ecf4-bb55-350b-a9e4-4dabe02f6269",
                                "text": "Afore night 'twur the talk o' all the parish, an' folk did run in an' out all day long for a week to look at un. An' I got a basket o 'apples an' a papern bag o' lollipops for the childern to carr' in my pocket. [...] But the lollipops had all a-melted drough the papern bag, an' he wur a-stickt to my pocket."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
